course: dictionary
lesson: 10071
title: Thankful: glad and grateful
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Thankful is an adjective, so it describes how a person feels. It can change to more thankful and most thankful. Someone who is thankful feels glad and grateful.
explain: Thankful can mean glad that something good happened, or glad that something bad did not happen. «Everyone was thankful that nobody was hurt.» The children were not hurt, so they feel glad and grateful about that.
explain: Thankful can also mean feeling thanks towards someone. Look at the words after it: «thankful for» shows what you feel grateful about, and «thankful that» introduces what happened. Context clue: «A photo that once made everyone cry... can one day make them smile: that is how grief changes into thankful love.» Grief is very sad, so thankful here must mean warm and grateful, the opposite of sorrow.
fact: Thankful is an adjective: «She felt thankful.»
fact: Thankful means glad and grateful.
fact: «Thankful that» is followed by something that happened: «thankful that the bridge was safe».
fact: «Thankful for» is followed by a thing or a person: «thankful for her help».
fact: At harvest festivals and at Thanksgiving in the USA and Canada, people say what they are thankful for.
exercise: «The family was thankful that nobody was hurt in the crash.» What does thankful mean here? | *Glad that something bad did not happen | Thirsty after the long drive | Angry with the driver | Sorry that the car was too small
exercise: Ella wrote a card to say she was ___ for her friend's help. Which word fits best? | thin | *thankful | thunderous | thirsty
exercise: «Lily was thankful for the warm coat on the cold morning.» What is Lily thankful for? | *The warm coat | The cold morning | The long bus ride | Her sister's shoes
test: «Sam was thankful that the bridge was still standing after the storm.» What does this tell you? | Sam was tired from walking across the bridge | Sam was frightened of the water below | Sam was angry that the bridge was built badly | *Sam was glad that something bad did not happen
test: Which phrase correctly shows that someone feels grateful towards a friend? | *thankful for your kindness | thankful your kindness | thankful that your kindness | thankful at your kindness
exam: Mum says, «We should be thankful for small mercies today.» What does she mean? | *We should feel grateful for small good things when times are hard | We should count every small mistake | We should be angry about the small weather | We should buy only small things today
